WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.530
- You can do some crazy stuff
with options like 10K to 90K

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.770
- [Narrator] Zero days to
expiration options, or 0DTE

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.470
have exploded in popularity
in the last year.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.810
They allow investors to
bet on stock market moves

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.160
within the same day,

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.280
which can result in big
wins and big losses.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.340
- This is one of the biggest
shifts I've seen in markets

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.570
of the past decade.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.180
- [Narrator] Here's why
0DTE options have taken off

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.980
despite being some of the
riskiest in the entire market.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.130
- So I got into 0DTE in 2020
during the whole like lockdown.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.007
- [Narrator] Drayson Little
graduated from college in 2021

00:00:35.007 --> 00:00:38.460
and has been trading options
full-time for about a year.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.750
He lives in Las Vegas,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.570
so his day typically
starts around 5:30 AM,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.390
an hour before the market
opens on the East Coast.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.223
- [Drayton] First things first,

00:00:46.223 --> 00:00:48.420
is I'll head over to Twitter,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.160
that's where I get all my news

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.360
- [Narrator] On big news days,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.190
like when inflation data is released,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.710
he says, "It's easier to
spot a trend in the market."

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.360
- [Drayton] You can see a massive move

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.340
into and from that PCE number

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.173
- [Narrator] Which he says,

00:01:00.173 --> 00:01:02.580
"Is the best time to trade 0DTE."

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.010
- In one minute, I had made $100.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.450
- [Narrator] He says, "He usually bets

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.310
a few thousand dollars per trade.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.050
One of his biggest one-day profits

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:14.460
was about $14,000, and biggest
loss was about $12,000."

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.550
- It's like euphoria, it's
like winning a lottery,

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.170
but then you also have your crazy lows.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.780
- [Narrator] 0DTE options
expire the same day

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.520
they're purchased,, which is why...

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.490
- They are some of the
most sensitive to changes

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.050
in the stock's price.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.390
So that's why you can see them zip higher

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.880
or crash incredibly quickly.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.440
- [Narrator] But that's
also part of the reason

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.150
they're so appealing to traders.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.830
- Your upside potential is infinite.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.560
It can be 500%, it could be 1000%.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.260
- [Narrator] Traders are
also drawn to 0DTE options

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.050
because they're cheaper
than longer-dated contracts.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:49.080
- But often the odds
are stacked against you.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.820
A lot of these retail traders

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.620
do end up losing a lot of money.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.960
- [Narrator] Drayson says,
"Some of his biggest losses

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.090
occurred in his first year of trading.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.080
- I think I probably lost
at the time during 2020,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.350
upwards of like $65,000,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.270
and this was when I was
a full-time student.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.650
I was an entrepreneur

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.890
before I had made some
money from E-commerce,

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.730
I lost 20, 30% of it, and it's just very,

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.460
it just feels really bad,
to be honest with you.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.710
- [Narrator] But he says,
"The possibility of big wins

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.390
enticed him to keep trading."

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.930
- The thing is, with a nine
to five, it's not scalable.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.720
You only make so much during these hours

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.960
compared to trading, where
you take one crazy trade,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.320
like just one trade and
you make a million dollars.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.790
- [Narrator] This type of options trading

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.800
has long been reserved for professionals

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.080
with sophisticated technology and tools.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.460
But in the last few years,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.560
retail traders have played a big role

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.010
in driving 0DTE trading
volumes to record highs.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.740
- It's really become a viral phenomenon.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.640
You know, when I was looking
at hashtags for 0DTE online,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.060
there are tens of thousands
of mentions of 0DTE,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.290
just this year alone.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.050
A few years ago, there
were no such mentions.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.300
- [Narrator] Part of the reason
is that options exchanges

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.170
expanded 0DTE contracts to
every day of the week last year

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.880
to capitalize on this boom.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.240
- And that just unleashed
a frenzy of activity.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.257
And traders I was talking to were saying,

00:03:14.257 --> 00:03:16.680
"We've never seen something take off

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.930
the way 0DTE trading has."

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.340
- [Narrator] Many of these retail traders

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.720
started with meme stocks.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.120
- This is really the
continuation of a trend

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.260
the past few years

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.970
as more people have entered markets

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.440
where they wanna bet on sports,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.670
they wanna bet at the casino,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.860
and they also wanna bet on stocks.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.000
- [Narrator] But some experts think

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.790
all this betting could mean
trouble for the market.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:36.870
- There's a lot of concern

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.750
from a lot of industry
analysts and pundits

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.360
that suggest that 0DTE
could kind of bring about

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.250
an end-of-day scenario in markets.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.110
- [Narrator] That's because
when professional traders

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.490
buy or sell options,

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.910
they also buy or sell stocks
to hedge their positions.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.130
- That creates worries that

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.200
if there is a big move in the market

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.250
and all of a sudden,

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.760
someone's doing a ton of
buying and selling of options

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.970
that could ripple over
into the stock market.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.100
- [Narrator] For example,
during the meme-stock mania,

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.110
there were concerns that options activity

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.120
was exacerbating the volatility.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.170
- I think a lot of the fear
now is that 0DTE volumes

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.390
will put the market in the same position.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.950
The odds of that happening is a lot lower

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.340
than in a situation like
GameStop or meme-mania.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.360
- [Narrator] While this concern

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.415
is hotly debated on Wall Street

00:04:23.415 --> 00:04:25.620
Kochuba says, "0DTE options

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.750
have become such a large part of trading,

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.330
that when there's an
unexplainable move in the market."

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.550
- You can look at the 0DTE volumes

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:35.070
and movement in 0DTE and understand that

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.950
this could be driving
those strange behaviors.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.060
- I wouldn't regret anything.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.860
I honestly find it,

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.020
it has taught me a lot more things

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.050
and has leveled me up as a person,

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.580
rather than pull me down.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.200
- [Narrator] With the
money he made from trading,

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.850
he says, 'He was able to buy...

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:55.080
- One of my dream cars, the
AMG GTR, get back to my family,

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.680
travel around the world,
and then I bought a Rolex.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.060
So that was pretty cool.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.740
- [Narrator] He says,
"His goal for next year

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.750
is to make six-figures every month

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.880
and launch an options trading course."

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.190
- You're gonna have your lows,
you're gonna have your highs,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.350
but as long as you just
keep moving forward,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.822
you'll eventually get to your end goal.

00:05:12.822 --> 00:05:15.405
(gentle music)

